<title>SPAIN: Spain's Erz H1 profits rise 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Erz H1 profits rise 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to end-June results for Endesa unit Electricas Reunidas de Zaragoza group in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Net attributable			   2.75  vs   2.69</p>
<p> Pretax profit				5.01  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Net taxed				    3.20  up   1.4 pct</p>
<p> Operating revenues			39.39  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Operating costs			   32.38  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Operating profit			   7.01  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Earnings per share (pesetas)	 141.43  vs 138.55</p>
<p> Financial revenues			 0.19  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Financial costs			    2.14  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Financial loss			     1.95  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Ordinary profit			    4.98  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Extraordinary income		     0.03  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Debt					  39.99  vs   n.a.</p>
<p> Investment in fixed assets	     2.00  vs   n.a.</p>
<p>NOTE: ERZ said electricity production rose 5.3 percent to 1.09 billion kwh, while its electricity market grew 1.9 percent to 2.6 billion kwh.</p>
<p>It distributed 478 million therms of gas in the period.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585-8341</p>
</text>
